# Iteration Artifacts Convention

All AIdLC and planned-iteration **documentation** lives under:

```text
dev/artifacts/iteration/{timestamp}-{micro-description}/
```

## Folder naming

| Part | Rule | Example |
|------|------|---------|
| `{timestamp}` | Unix epoch seconds (10 digits) at iteration start | `1783016581` |
| `{micro-description}` | Lowercase kebab-case, 2–5 words, no spaces | `code-quality-security-hardening` |

**Full example:** `1783016581-code-quality-security-hardening`

Generate timestamp at folder creation:

```powershell
$ts = [int][double]::Parse((Get-Date -UFormat %s))
$folder = "artifacts/iteration/${ts}-your-short-name"
```

## Required layout (inside each iteration folder)

```text
{timestamp}-{micro-description}/
  README.md              # Iteration summary (scope, dates, status)
  aidlc-state.md         # Workflow state
  audit.md               # Append-only interaction log
  inception/             # Requirements, design, plans
  construction/          # Units, build-and-test, sign-off
  operations/            # Optional placeholder
```

## Rules

1. **Never** put application code in iteration folders — only docs/markdown.
2. **One folder per iteration** — do not mix two iterations in one directory.
3. **New iteration = new folder** — do not overwrite a completed iteration folder.
4. **audit.md** — append only; never overwrite entire file.
5. Point `aidlc-docs/README.md` or index to the current/latest iteration path.

## When starting work

1. Create `artifacts/iteration/{timestamp}-{slug}/` first.
2. Initialize `aidlc-state.md` and `audit.md`.
3. Log all workflow output under that folder, not under `aidlc-docs/` root.
